  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Caramelised onion chutney takes longer than the red onion version because white onions need a full 40 to 50 minutes of slow cooking before they darken properly. The result is a deep, rich, deeply savoury preserve,  almost brown-sugar dark,  that pairs with strong cheese, beef, and anything in need of a sweet counterpoint. Makes about three 300 g jars."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
